simple_tp and mc_axis side by side: both in one thread, one target (a step
plus a ramp moving inside the thread), one enable, one maxvel/maxaccel.
mc_axis runs as a virtual axis in track mode (mode 3), wired as in "REPLACING SIMPLE_TP" of
mc_axis(9); sampler records every period of both planners.

Inputs: steps from rest, a reversal while moving, enable 0 in the middle of a
move and again at rest, maxvel lowered and maxvel/maxaccel raised during a
move, a target moving at 20 units/s, and the same target moving again after
the planners reached it.

Checked on the record: neither planner exceeds maxvel (except while ramping
down to a lowered maxvel) or maxaccel; neither passes a standing target;
wherever simple_tp comes to rest at a standing target, mc_axis is at rest
there too, at most 2 periods later (the two planners discretise the same
stopping law differently at the start and at the end of a move).

MCTP_MODE=0 runs mc_axis as MC_MoveAbsolute with ContinuousUpdate instead:
the move ends Done at the first standing target, so it does not follow the
next one and the test fails.  Every wait is on a HAL state; test.sh bounds
the whole test.

cmpj.hal / cmpj.py: the same with a jerk limit.  simple_tp.comp has no jerk
input; the simple_tp that plans with max_jerk is the jog planner of motion,
src/emc/motion/simple_tp.c (S-curve, planner type 1).  test.sh builds it into
ref_simple_tp (as tests/blendmath does); mc_axis runs in HAL (track mode, the
jerk input = maxjerk), sampler records its inputs and outputs, and the inputs
are replayed period by period through simple_tp.c.  Inputs: steps from rest,
a reversal while moving, a nearer target while moving, enable 0 mid-move and
1 again, a target moving at 20 units/s, a step with maxjerk 1000, steps of
0.001, 0.00001 and 0.000017.  Checked: mc_axis keeps maxvel, maxaccel and maxjerk (from its
recorded velocity, with the 6-decimal resolution of halsampler); it never
passes a standing target and comes to rest exactly on it; its position
differs from simple_tp.c by at most TOL = maxvel * 1.5 periods in every
period (cmpj.py says where the 1.5 periods come from).  Not compared: maxvel
lowered during a move, which simple_tp.c obeys in one period (its velocity
is clipped, not ramped).
